{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 5. Ne5. Nf3 prevents an immediate queen check on h4. Black uses ...g5 to keep f4, so h4 attacks the supporting chain. After ...g4 the knight must move; Ne5 takes an active central post. Black can play ...Nf6 against e4 and ...d6 against Ne5. Count the defenders of e4 before chasing f7. } 5. Ne5 Nf6 6. d4 d6 7. Nd3 Nxe4 *

