{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 8. Bxf4. The retreat Nd3 keeps the knight protected and allows the bishop to recover f4. Black takes e4, so material recovery alone has not won the opening. Black's knight is active and your king remains central. A speculative attack on f7 can lose time against ...Bg7 and ...O-O. } 8. Bxf4 Qe7 9. Be2 Nc6 10. Nc3 Nxc3 *

