{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 6. Nxg4. Black attacks Ne5 with the d-pawn, but the knight can capture the advanced g4 pawn while escaping. This concrete resource is stronger than mechanically retreating to d3 in this exact position. A similar position with an extra black developing move can change the tactics. Do not treat Nxg4 as universal whenever ...d6 attacks Ne5. } 6. Nxg4 Nc6 7. Nc3 Nf6 8. Nxf6+ Qxf6 *

