{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 5. hxg5. White captures on g5 immediately, testing the supporting pawn chain before building d4. The exact recapture matters because the h-file and rook on h8 can become tactically relevant. Black may develop with ...Bg7 or use the center. A careless capture can open a rook line against an undeveloped position. } 5. hxg5 Bg7 6. gxh6 Rxh6 7. Rxh6 Bxh6 *

