{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. Choose the course move, explain its purpose and name one opposing resource. Other playable moves may exist; this is a repertoire-recall question. ANSWER: Course move: 6. Ng1. Black's ...d6 controls e5, so the Kieseritzky knight jump is unavailable. Ng1 is a deliberate retreat preserving the knight after the g-pawn advance. Playing Ne5 as if ...d6 were absent simply leaves the knight vulnerable. Black also threatens to complete development while you spend another knight tempo. } 6. Ng1 Qf6 7. Nc3 Ne7 8. Nge2 Bh6 *

